# The set commands the brief lists, their refusals and the wrong type — endpoint-sets, without SSCAN.
# A set's order is not Redis's (research D-22) and Redis promises none: replies of several members are
# [unordered]. Random replies are [random <population>]: members of it, as many as Redis's, both held.
# After a random SPOP the two servers hold different members, so later lines on that key read counts.
FLUSHALL
SADD post:9:tags kotlin native kotlin
SISMEMBER post:9:tags kotlin
SISMEMBER post:9:tags java
SCARD post:9:tags
[unordered] SMEMBERS post:9:tags
TYPE post:9:tags
SADD s m0 m1 m2 m3 m4 m5 m6 m7 m8 m9
[random m0 m1 m2 m3 m4 m5 m6 m7 m8 m9] SRANDMEMBER s 3
[random m0 m1 m2 m3 m4 m5 m6 m7 m8 m9] SRANDMEMBER s -20
[random m0 m1 m2 m3 m4 m5 m6 m7 m8 m9] SRANDMEMBER s
[random m0 m1 m2 m3 m4 m5 m6 m7 m8 m9] SRANDMEMBER s 1
[random m0 m1 m2 m3 m4 m5 m6 m7 m8 m9] SRANDMEMBER s -1
[unordered] SRANDMEMBER s 100
[unordered] SRANDMEMBER s 10
SRANDMEMBER s 0
SRANDMEMBER s x
SRANDMEMBER s -9223372036854775808
SRANDMEMBER s 1 2
SRANDMEMBER
SRANDMEMBER nokey
SRANDMEMBER nokey 5
SRANDMEMBER nokey -5
SRANDMEMBER nokey x
SRANDMEMBER nokey 0
SCARD s
SMISMEMBER s m1 nope m2
